# Known-safe findings, pinned individually.
#
# The secret scan runs over the FULL history on every push (see ci.yml, which
# explains why). Two test fixtures trip the generic-api-key rule on entropy
# alone, so the job has been failing on every push — and a control that is
# always red is not a control: the next genuine leak arrives as one more red
# run that nobody looks at twice. That is the actual risk being fixed here,
# not the noise.
#
# These are FINGERPRINTS (commit:file:rule:line), not path or regex
# allowlists, and that is deliberate. An allowlist like `test/**` or "any
# 64-hex string in a test file" would also hide a real key committed to a test
# tomorrow, which is a normal way for keys to leak. A fingerprint exempts one
# known line in one known commit and nothing else.
#
# Verify before adding to this file. Both below were checked, not assumed.

# The public CRED token contract on Base, in a captured permit2 payload used as
# a test fixture. A contract address is public by definition — it is in
# assets.ts and on Basescan. Flagged for entropy, not for being secret.
